It's that time of year when drugstore candy aisles fill with red hearts, the price of a dozen roses seems to skyrocket, and people's thoughts turn to the state of their romantic relationship or their lack of one. For psychologists, romance, attraction, and love are not merely the stuff of poetry. They're subjects for scientific study. What are the qualities of a successful relationship? Why do some relationships last and others fail? What do we gain from our relationships and how do we know which ones are we? worth holding on to. These are some of the questions that relationship scientists delve into, and their research can help the rest of us
每年的这个时候，药店的糖果货架上都会摆满红色的心形装饰，一打玫瑰花的价格似乎也飞涨起来，人们开始思考自己的恋爱关系状况，或者思考自己为何处于单身状态。对于心理学家来说，浪漫、吸引力和爱情不仅仅是诗歌的素材，它们也是科学研究的对象。一段成功的关系具备哪些特质？为什么有些关系能长久，而有些却以失败告终？我们从关系中获得了什么？我们如何知道哪些关系值得坚持？这些都是关系科学家深入研究的问题，他们的研究可以帮助我们其他人

