polling center, we did a poll early on in the pandemic in May. And when we ask people, you know, how do you think the pandemic is going to affect your relationship? There's a lot of optimism. 51% said that they thought the pandemic was going to make their relationship stronger. And that's completely counterintuitive to what a lot of people thought at the time. Only 1% thought it was going to have gotten worse. 1%? 1%, right? So it's like, one out of 100 thought, you know, this is going to be bad for us.
民意调查中心，我们在疫情早期的五月份进行了一次民意调查。当我们问人们：“你认为疫情会如何影响你的关系？”时，人们表现出了很多乐观情绪。51%的人认为疫情会让他们的关系变得更稳固。这与当时许多人的想法完全相反。只有1%的人认为关系会变差。1%？是的，1%。所以就像是100个人里只有1个人认为这对我们来说会很糟糕。

