we're looking might go a long way to help people, you know, do better during during these troubling times. More generally, what have you and other researchers found are the most important qualities or ingredients that make relationships work? Some research done by Rhonda Balzorini and many colleagues, cleverly titled Love in the time of COVID, found that, you know, COVID has been very stressful for lots of people. But what they found was when one of the partners was very responsive. And so a responsive partner is someone who listens to you.
可能会在很大程度上帮助人们在这些困难时期过得更好。更广泛地说，您和其他研究人员发现，让关系维持下去的最重要品质或要素是什么？由朗达·巴尔佐里尼（Rhonda Balzorini）和许多同事进行的一项研究，巧妙地命名为《新冠时期的爱》（Love in the time of COVID），发现新冠疫情对许多人来说压力很大。但他们发现，当其中一方非常善于回应时——所谓善于回应的伴侣，是指那些倾听你、

