cares what you think and tries to see things from your perspective. It really helped mitigate a lot of the stress that COVID has brought on. So being one of those partners who really takes the time to understand, validate and care for each other is really going to help your relationship weather the storm. You did an interesting poll a few years ago where you asked people whether their partner was their best friend, and you found that 83% said yes, a far higher number than in a similar survey 25 years earlier. Why do you think that's changed? I think we're getting better at relationships. I think we're expecting more, and rightfully so.
关心你的想法并试图从你的角度看问题的人——这确实有助于减轻新冠带来的许多压力。因此，成为那种真正花时间去理解、认可和关心彼此的伴侣，真的会帮助你们的关系度过难关。几年前，您做了一项有趣的民意调查，询问人们他们的伴侣是否是他们最好的朋友，结果发现83%的人回答“是”，这个数字远高于25年前的类似调查。您认为为什么会发生这种变化？我认为我们在处理关系方面变得更好了。我认为我们期望更高，这是理所应当的。

