relationships than we think we are. You describe a study where college students were less accurate at predicting how long their current relationships would last than their parents or roommates were. Why is that? Is love truly blind? Yeah, it's also a little deaf, a little dumb. Yeah, I mean, that study shows, you know, you ask people, to look off into the future and what's your relationship going to be like.
