And really what happens is your parents, You know, it's parents, but it's really mostly moms and your roommate have some other information that you don't necessarily in the sense that they're not in love with your partner. And so when you're in love, you're making decisions for more emotional side. Your roommate knows what you've told them, but also sees some of the fallout perhaps of a bad experience you had with a partner, a fight, or, you know, perhaps crying in your room. those kinds of things. They have that inside information. And so both, particularly your mom and your roommate to a large extent, just want what's best for you. They don't really care about your partner's feelings. And so a lot of times in relationships, we get really wrapped up and convinced that we're doing a lot of things that aren't good for us for our partner. And that's ultimately going to be
实际上发生的情况是，你的父母——你知道，主要是妈妈——和你的室友拥有一些你未必拥有的信息，因为他们并没有爱上你的伴侣。所以当你坠入爱河时，你的决定更多是出于情感层面。你的室友知道你告诉过他们的事情，但也可能看到了你与伴侣糟糕经历的一些后果，比如争吵，或者，你知道，可能在房间里哭泣，诸如此类的事情。他们拥有那些内部信息。因此，无论是你的妈妈还是你的室友，在很大程度上，他们只是想要对你最好的。他们并不真正关心你伴侣的感受。所以很多时候在关系中，我们变得非常投入，并确信我们正在做很多对我们和伴侣并不好的事情。而这最终会

